script:
// Visuals come from surface / iconSize; instance background, corner, border, shadow and clip land on the 44pt hit-area
// root and do not restyle the circle.
// NavButton (Stratoapp DesignSystem NavGlassButton): a 44pt circle (layoutMetrics.minimumTouchTarget) around a template-tinted
// icon in textPrimary (= el16). back = NavGlassButton.back: @icon.back (NavigationBarBackIndicator = SF arrow.left) at
// NavGlassMetrics.backIconSide 16; other icons NavGlassMetrics.iconSide 20. surface glass = navGlassSurface(Circle()):
// FrostGlassBackground(blurStyle .thin, tintOpacity 0, shadow .chatGlass = chatGlassShadow r18 y4) under a 1pt (hairlineWidth)
// navGlassStroke ring; plain = no surface. Press: scale 0.96 + opacity 0.9 (PressScaleButtonStyle, not under Reduce Motion) and
// the selection haptic. `label` is the a11y label (the button has no text).
// The icon primitive insets the glyph 1/12 per side (Android drawables carry that padding, SF Symbols don't) while the native
// frames it edge to edge, so the icon node is iconSize × 6/5.
// ponytail: the native surface is glassEffect(.regular) on iOS 26 (.ultraThinMaterial before) and the primitives have no
// Liquid Glass or ultra-thin material, so the layer is `material: thin` under a bg1Elevated veil at 0.77 — measured against
// the native button on bg1 (iPhone 17 Pro, iOS 26.5): light 252 = 252, dark 33 vs 25 (the native dark circle is the backdrop
// plus a specular rim). Android draws a translucent bg1 fill under the same veil.
param icon: icon
param label: string = ""
param iconSize: number = 20
param surface: "glass" | "plain" = "glass"
event tap
